Z||000000||Fearless Freep||10-01-2000||06:10 PM||||Was crawling around under the driver side (checking fuses etc.) and suddenly noticed that the carpet/padding way in the back up and behind the fuse area was wet!  Okay....so whats in that area and what do I check.......guess Im looking at re-doing the carpet just to find the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-01-2000||07:21 PM||||run some water on the windshield. you could have a leak below there. it could also come thru a hole in the floor. you'll have to dig around.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||10-01-2000||08:30 PM||||Was it water or was it hydraulic fluid from one of the master cylinders there? The clutch master cylinder often leaks (not applicable to automatics!).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fearless Freep||10-01-2000||08:39 PM||||Ed....<P>I never thought of that (sudden shivers)...stuck my fingers all in it and it didnt have a funny smell....hmmmmm I had just washed the car.......Im gonna have to stick my hand in it again...||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||10-02-2000||12:24 AM||||Do you have a sunroof?  If so check the rubber seals around the latch and hinge hardware.  The old ones had separate washers and they crack with time.  The new replacements (still available from the dealer for under $20) have the bolts with an integral seal.<P>Water can trickle through the front hinge hardware, run along the lip of the sunroof, down the windshield pillar and end up on the carpet near the fuse panel.<P>Worth taking a look.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
